{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Da6Vx1Q6bv8diof3rjFbF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment reimplementing GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: cmd/ (one package per utility), pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness), pkg/sys/ (syscall abstractions), pkg/format/ (output formatting), magefiles/ (build automation), docs/ (specs/SRDs).\n\n**Current state**: 114 SRDs specified, all releases 00.0–15.0 at spec_complete status. Generation run 44 is in progress. Recent commits completed sort requirements through R4.1 (tasks 5376 and 5377). Many utilities are implemented; many remain.\n\n**Current release focus**: Release 07.0 (sort, tr, tail) is the earliest release with ready requirements. Sort has 3 remaining requirements (R4.2–R4.4). tr (14 requirements) and tail (15 requirements) have not started.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 07.0 is the earliest incomplete release with ready R-items:\n- **srd053-sort**: R4.2, R4.3, R4.4 (3 ready) — partially implemented, needs completion\n- **srd054-tr**: R1.1–R4.3 (14 ready) — not started\n- **srd055-tail**: R1.1–R4.4 (15 ready) — not started\n\nNo dependencies between these three utilities. Sort is partially built and should be completed first. tr and tail can start in parallel.\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\nAssuming default weight=1 per requirement (no weight overrides visible in project context):\n\n- Task 0: sort R4.2(w=1) + R4.3(w=1) + R4.4(w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 1: tail R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 2: tr R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n- Task 3: tr R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) + R2.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nAll within budget.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/sort: final features -- srd053 R4.2-R4.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd053-sort.yaml (full SRD -- read requirements R4.2, R4.3, R4.4)\n      - cmd/sort/main.go (existing implementation -- R1.1 through R4.1 are already implemented)\n      - cmd/sort/sort_test.go (existing differential tests to extend)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness -- BuildBinary and RunDiffTests usage)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sort/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add features for R4.2, R4.3, R4.4\n      - path: cmd/sort/sort_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R4.2, R4.3, R4.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd053 R4.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd053 R4.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd053 R4.4 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing cmd/sort implementation. Requirements R1.1 through R4.1 are already implemented in main.go. Read the existing code to understand the current structure before adding features.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the Env field of each DiffTest.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use gsort as the reference binary name for exec.LookPath. Call t.Skip if gsort is not found.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/sort/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/sort/ -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if gsort is not in PATH)\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/sort/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"All three SRD requirements (R4.2, R4.3, R4.4) are implemented and exercised by differential test cases\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/tail: basic tail output -- srd055 R1.1-R1.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd055-tail.yaml (full SRD -- read requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness -- BuildBinary and RunDiffTests usage pattern)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler function)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/tail/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"tail implementation covering R1.1-R1.4: basic last-N-lines output from stdin and files\"\n      - path: cmd/tail/tail_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go binary against gtail reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd055 R1.1 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd055 R1.2 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd055 R1.3 as specified in the SRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd055 R1.4 as specified in the SRD\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main to match GNU coreutils behavior when piped to consumers that close stdin early.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use the differential testing pattern: testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") for the Go binary, exec.LookPath(\\\"gtail\\\") for the reference binary, t.Skip if reference not found.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the Env field of each DiffTest.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"This is the initial implementation. Later tasks will add R2.x-R4.x features. Structure the code so flag parsing and core logic are separable for future extension.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/tail/ compiles without errors\"\n